==Opening ceremony==
[[File:KillersBST080717-38 (35742625041) (cropped) (cropped).jpg|thumb|American rock band [[The Killers]] ''(pictured in 2017)'' were announced to perform at the 2026 UEFA Champions League final's opening ceremony.]]
On 26 March 2026, American [[indie rock]] band [[The Killers]] were announced as the performers for the final's [[Pepsi]] opening ceremony, and was promoted by a trailer starring Killers frontman [[Brandon Flowers]] and football star [[David Beckham]] on a short film named ''The Race Begins''.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/02a3-203c92120410-1facdfda4b60-1000--the-killers-to-headline-uefa-champions-league-final-kick-of/ |title=The Killers to headline UEFA Champions League Final Kick Off Show by Pepsi® |date=29 March 2026|access-date=16 April 2026 |website=UEFA.com}}</ref>

==Match==
===Summary===
{{multiple image
 | align = right
 | direction = horizontal
 | total_width = 300
 | image1 = Vitinha USMNT v Portugal Mar 31 2026-50 (cropped).jpg
 | image2 = 1 kai havertz 2026 (cropped).jpg
 | footer = Paris Saint-Germain midfielder [[Vitinha (footballer, born February 2000)|Vitinha]] (left) was named [[Player of the match#Association football|man of the match]], while his opponent midfielder [[Kai Havertz]] (right) scored the earliest goal of the match.
}}

In the sixth minute of the match, an attempted [[glossary_of_association_football_terms#C|clearance]] by Paris Saint-Germain defender [[Marquinhos]] deflected off Arsenal's [[Leandro Trossard]]. The deflected ball fell to Arsenal striker [[Kai Havertz]], who beat the Paris Saint-Germain goalkeeper [[Matvey Safonov]] from a tight angle, putting Arsenal 1–0 ahead. It would be their only shot on target throughout the match.<ref>{{Cite web |title=PSG beat Arsenal on penalties to defend Champions League title |url=https://www.espn.com/football/report/_/gameId/401862897 |date=30 May 2026 |access-date=5 June 2026 |website=ESPN }}</ref>

In the 61st minute, Arsenal's [[Cristhian Mosquera]] fouled [[Khvicha Kvaratskhelia]] inside the [[penalty box]]. [[Ousmane Dembélé]] converted the resulting penalty kick, tying the score at 1–1. In the 77th minute, a shot by Kvaratskhelia was deflected onto the post by [[Myles Lewis-Skelly]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Rouse |first1=Daniel |title=Champions League final analysis: PSG beat Arsenal on penalties |url=https://www.thescore.com/chlg/news/3547570/champions-league-final-analysis-psg-beat-arsenal-on-penalties |access-date=10 June 2026 |work=TheScore |date=30 May 2026}}</ref> By the end of the second half, Paris Saint-Germain had made 18 attempts on goal (four on target), while Arsenal had made four attempts (one on target). With the score still tied, the game went to [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]].

In the 103rd minute, Paris Saint-Germain's [[Nuno Mendes (footballer, born 2002)|Nuno Mendes]] tackled [[Noni Madueke]] to the ground in his team's penalty area, prompting appeals for a penalty kick by Arsenal players. However, the referee awarded a [[free kick]] to Paris Saint-Germain instead, adjudging that Madueke had grabbed Mendes' arm,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Davies |first1=Andy |title=VAR review: UCL ref got the Mendes-Madueke call right, but it was close |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/48923039/var-review-ucl-ref-got-mendes-madueke-call-right-was-close |access-date=10 June 2026 |date=30 May 2026|website=ESPN}}</ref> and issued [[Penalty_card#Association_football|yellow card]]s to Arsenal player [[Declan Rice]] and manager [[Mikel Arteta]] for their protests.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hewitt |first1=Matthew |title=Declan Rice and Mikel Arteta explode as Arsenal denied Champions League final penalty |url=https://www.football.london/arsenal-fc/news/arsenal-champions-league-final-psg-34038721 |access-date=10 June 2026 |work=football.London |date=30 May 2026}}</ref> Extra time ended with the score tied 1–1 and the match proceeded to a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]].

Paris Saint-Germain went first in the shoot-out, with [[Gonçalo Ramos]] converting his penalty. This was followed by successful attempts by Arsenal's [[Viktor Gyökeres]] and Paris Saint-Germain's [[Désiré Doué]]. The first miss was by Arsenal's [[Eberechi Eze]], who shot wide left, which was immediately followed by Arsenal goalkeeper [[David Raya]] saving Mendes' attempt. Four successful attempts followed, two for each team, by Rice, [[Achraf Hakimi]], [[Gabriel Martinelli]], and [[Lucas Beraldo]], leaving Paris Saint-Germain ahead 4–3 with one penalty attempt to come before the [[Sudden death (sport)|sudden-death round]]. [[Gabriel Magalhães|Gabriel]] sent his shot over the bar, giving Paris Saint-Germain the victory.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/report/_/gameId/401862897 |access-date=2026-06-01|website=ESPN|date=May 30, 2026|title=PSG 1-1 Arsenal (May 30, 2026) Game Analysis}}</ref>

